    {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "change": "The pension intake question is now owner-scoped. It asked \"in your own name\", which is why a confirmed spouse's pension was never sought: the requirement knew whose pension was missing, but the spoken question threw that away and asked the primary client again. The prompt now comes from the owner-scoped need, and names buyout bond rather than AVC because a buyout bond is a distinct position the projection models and cannot be paid into. Only the pension prompt changes: unscoped questions keep their existing conversational wording, and nextQuestion still agrees with the brief.",
